{
  "title": "VectorAction",
  "description": "A named two-dimensional input, fed by a stick, by four direction buttons, or by several such bindings at once. Each alternative binding is evaluated as a whole vector and the longest one wins, so x never comes from the keyboard while y comes from the pad. The result is clamped to unit length rather than normalized: a digital diagonal is no faster than a cardinal direction, while analog input below full deflection keeps its magnitude.",
